    "title": "Bulldogs blast Cardinals in volleyball - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Brian Bowman ,\n14 hours ago\nThe Swanville Bulldogs defeated the Upsala Cardinals 3-0 by scores of 25-16, 25-13, and 25-17 in volleyball play on Tuesday, Sept. 30.\n“The girls played very well tonight,” Bulldogs’ head coach Luke Peterson said in an email. “We cleaned up some of the missed serves we have been having and that helped us build nice leads in each set.”\nSwanville’s Avery Douglas had a historic night, reaching the career milestone of 2,000 digs.\n“I’m so proud of her,” Peterson said. “She was part of the first class of 8th graders when I started coaching and has worked so hard to get to this point in her career - such an amazing player and young lady.”\nSwanville 3 Walker-Hackensack-Akeley 0\nSwanville also defeated Walker-Hackensack Akeley 3-0 by scores of 25-19, 25-20, and 25-23 on Monday, Sept. 29.\n“The girls played a good game,” Peterson said. “Our defense was solid and we passed well which helped us transition to offense quickly.”\nOn Thursday, Sept. 25, Swanville swept Osakis 3-0, winning by scores of 25-20, 25-21, and 25-19.\n“Our defense was great tonight,” Peterson said. “We were moving our feet and were able to transition well.”\nThe Bulldogs' team statistics from the match included eight service aces, 0 serve-receive errors, six blocks, and 34 kills.\nSwanville played Browerville-Eagle Valley on Thursday, Oct. 2, but no score was available at press time.\nThe Bulldogs will host Bertha-Hewitt on Monday, Oct. 6 and Benson Tuesday, Oct. 7. Both games will start at 7:15 p.m.",
